            "The moneylender is the opposite in every way. He knows his borrowers personally, so he is often willing to lend without any collateral at all, and a borrower can approach him again even without having repaid the earlier loan. But look at what that costs. He charges very high rates of interest, he keeps no records of the transactions, and he harasses the poor borrowers.",
            "The self-help group is the way around that. Fifteen to twenty people from one neighbourhood — usually women — organise themselves into a group.",
